Package: MetaScreener
Type: Package
Title: Directional Meta-Analysis of Gene-Set Activity across Multiple Datasets
    and Enrichment Methods
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Dingkang", "Zhao", , "dingkang.25@intl.zju.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantifies the direction of gene-set activity rather than only
    testing whether an association exists. For every candidate signature the
    package scores activity in each cohort with a panel of enrichment and
    scoring methods (GSVA, ssGSEA, z-score, PLAGE, PCA, AUCell, UCell,
    singscore, MEDIAN, FGSEA, ORA, UDT, ULM, VIPER and weighted variants),
    tests the resulting scores with parametric, non-parametric and resampling
    statistics, converts the two-sided p-values into one-sided activation and
    inhibition evidence according to the sign of the effect, and combines that
    evidence across methods and across datasets with twelve p-value
    combination strategies. The output is an Activation Direction Index (ADI)
    and an Inhibition Direction Index (IDI) per signature, so that signatures
    can be ranked by how consistently, and in which direction, they respond to
    a phenotype.
